  "id": "event-related-potential",
  "term": "event-related potential",
  "definition": "An event-related potential is a neurophysiological measure used to study cognitive processing. In this packet, it refers to brain-response patterns described by features such as amplitude, latency, global field power, and topographic distribution, which can reveal processing differences even when behaviour looks similar.",
